{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Brings.brings_is_qou","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Brings.brings_is_qou","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Int.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.brings_is_qou","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.brings_is_qou","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/brings_is_qou.lean#L47-L79","doc":"**Content statement** (from manuscript).\n\nBring's surface $\\Sigma_4$ ([Bring's surface](#def\\:brings-surface))\ngives rise to a quantum observable universe over $R$ (with\n$30 \\in R^{\\times}$).  The five sub-claims:\n\n(i) Quantum universe — the realisation is $\\mathbf{C} = \\mathrm{Rep}(\\mathrm{SU}_q(2))$,\n    i.e. quantum-group arity $2$;\n(ii) Observability — $\\dim \\mathrm{Hom}(\\mathbf 1, \\mathrm{Ad}\\,A) = 0$\n    (quantum Schur lemma);\n(iii) Yekutieli lifting — the obstruction $\\kappa_n$ vanishes exactly for\n    $n \\mid 6$ and persists for $n \\nmid 6$ (derived from the Kummer degree\n    condition, the lone open categorical input, carried by `[BringsObstruction]`);\n(iv) Euler characteristic — $g = 4$ and $\\chi(A) = 2 - 2g = -6$\n    (**derived** arithmetic);\n(v) Geometric descent (Riemann–Hurwitz) — $6$ branch points, total\n    ramification $14$.\n\nOnly the degree condition behind sub-claim (iii) is assumed; (i), (ii), (iv), (v) are discharged by\n`norm_num` / `rfl`.  In particular `χ(A) = -6` is *derived* from\n`χ(A) = 2 - 2·4`, not asserted independently. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:brings-is-qou","label":"prop:brings-is-qou","md":"quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-is-qou.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BringsObstruction.kummer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BringsObstruction.kummer","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/brings_is_qou.lean#L45-L45","doc":"Kummer degree condition: `κ_n = 0 ↔ n ∣ χ(A) = 2 - 2g`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BringsObstruction.genus_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BringsObstruction.genus_eq","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/brings_is_qou.lean#L43-L43","doc":"Bring's surface has genus 4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BringsObstruction.genus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BringsObstruction.genus","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/brings_is_qou.lean#L41-L41","doc":"Genus of the surface. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BringsObstruction.kappa","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BringsObstruction.kappa","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/brings_is_qou.lean#L39-L39","doc":"Obstruction classes `κ_n` indexed by jet level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BringsObstruction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BringsObstruction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/brings_is_qou.lean#L37-L37","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BringsObstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BringsObstruction","kind":"class","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/brings_is_qou.lean#L32-L45","doc":"The one genuinely-open categorical input for `brings_is_qou`: the\n**Kummer degree condition** for the Yekutieli jet obstruction on Bring's\nsurface — the level-`n` class `κ_n` vanishes exactly when `n ∣ χ(A)`,\nwhere `χ(A) = 2 - 2g` and `g = 4`. A categorical proof is open (the §3b\nconjectural hypothesis); which levels are obstructed is *derived*. ","signatureChunk":0}]}